BT /F2 17 Tf 54 730.0 Td (Artificial Intelligence Acceptable-Use Policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise \(HPE\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 683.0 Td (Document Owner: Chief Information Security Officer \(CISO\), in partnership with the Office of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 669.0 Td (General Counsel and the Chief Digital & Technology Office) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 655.0 Td (Status: Board-Approved | Version 3.0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641.0 Td (Effective Date: 8 July 2026 | Next Review: July 2027) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 621.0 Td (---) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 595.0 Td (1. Purpose and Board Approval) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 572.0 Td (Generative AI \(GenAI\) tools offer meaningful productivity, engineering, and innovation benefits to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558.0 Td (Hewlett Packard Enterprise. This Acceptable-Use Policy establishes the guardrails that allow HPE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 544.0 Td (team members to adopt these tools responsibly while protecting our data, our customers, our) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 530.0 Td (intellectual property, and our reputation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 510.0 Td (This policy was reviewed and approved by the HPE Board of Directors upon the recommendation of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 496.0 Td (Audit Committee and the Executive AI Governance Council. Board approval reflects the strategic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 482.0 Td (importance of trustworthy AI at HPE and gives this policy authority across the enterprise. It will) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 468.0 Td (remain in force until superseded by a subsequent board-approved revision.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 442.0 Td (2. Scope and Applicability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 419.0 Td (This policy applies to all HPE employees, contractors, consultants, interns, and third parties) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 405.0 Td (\(collectively, "team members"\) who access HPE systems, data, or networks. Its scope covers the use) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 391.0 Td (of all public, commercial, and internally hosted GenAI assistants and large-language-model services) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 377.0 Td (in the course of HPE business, whether accessed on HPE-managed devices, personal devices, or through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 363.0 Td (cloud services. It applies globally across all business units, functions, and geographies, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 349.0 Td (supplements-rather than replaces-HPE's Standards of Business Conduct, Information Security Policy,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 335.0 Td (Data Classification Standard, and Privacy Policy.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 309.0 Td (3. Sanctioned Tools and Authorization) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 286.0 Td (Only GenAI tools that have received formal authorization and sign-off through HPE's AI intake and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 272.0 Td (review process may be used for company work. Sanctioning requires security, privacy, and legal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 258.0 Td (assessment, and enterprise agreements that protect HPE data \(for example, contractual assurances) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 244.0 Td (that inputs are not used to train public models\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 224.0 Td (The following tools are currently sanctioned for the uses described in their onboarding guidance:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 204.0 Td (- Microsoft 365 Copilot - for drafting, summarizing, and analysis within HPE's licensed M365) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 190.0 Td (  tenant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 176.0 Td (- GitHub Copilot - for approved software engineering teams, subject to secure-coding and IP) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 162.0 Td (  review controls.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 148.0 Td (- ChatGPT Enterprise - for general-purpose assistance under HPE's enterprise agreement.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 128.0 Td (Free or personal-tier versions of ChatGPT, Copilot, or any other public assistant are not authorized) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 114.0 Td (for HPE business. Introducing any unapproved GenAI tool, browser extension, or model API constitutes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 100.0 Td (shadow AI and is prohibited. Requests for new tools must be submitted to the AI Governance Council) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 86.0 Td (for approval before use; procurement or expensing of AI services also requires this sign-off.) Tj ET
endstream
